:{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximalCliques(checkedContaining:)","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalcliques(checkedcontaining:)","abstract":[{"text":"The maximal cliques containing ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", throwing instead of trapping when it is not a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex of the graph.","type":"text"}],"title":"maximalCliques(checkedContaining:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximalCliques","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"checkedContaining","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"VertexNotFound","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols14VertexNotFoundV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MaximalCliques","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"}}}